"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols"]]},"references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/cliqueNumber()":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/cliquenumber()","title":"cliqueNumber()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cliqueNumber"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The size of a largest clique of the simple graph, ω: 0 for the empty graph, 1 for an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edgeless one, at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"coreNumbers().degeneracy + 1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Branch and bound in degeneracy order,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each vertex’s later neighbors (at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"degeneracy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", those with a high enough core number)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as the candidates, one search per vertex that raises the best size as it goes, pruned by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counts and a greedy coloring, stopping at the degeneracy bound. Exponential in the worst","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"case; memory O(n + m + degeneracy²).","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/cliqueNumber()","role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/clusteringCoefficients()":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/clusteringcoefficients()","title":"clusteringCoefficients()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clusteringCoefficients","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques22ClusteringCoefficientsV","text":"ClusteringCoefficients","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Triangles and clustering for every vertex of the simple graph (self-loops ignored,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parallel edges counted once), in one compact-forward pass. O(m^(3\/2))."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/clusteringCoefficients()","role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximumClique()":{"kind":"symbol","title":"maximumClique()","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumClique()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximumclique()","abstract":[{"text":"The lexicographically least largest clique by vertex index, in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order; [] for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored. Each largest clique is searched for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from its first vertex in degeneracy order, among that vertex’s later neighbors, so memory","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stays O(n + m + degeneracy²) however large a hub’s degree; of two cliques of one size, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lesser is the one holding the least vertex of their symmetric difference. Exponential in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"worst case.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumClique"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/averageClustering()":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/averageclustering()","title":"averageClustering()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"averageClustering","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The mean local clustering coefficient over every vertex, zeros included, summed in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order; 0 when empty.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/averageClustering()","role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","title":"Graph","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"abstract":[{"text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"between them. Kept apart from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"text":": an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one, and no type is both. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directed"},{"text":" views it as one when an algorithm needs arcs.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/transitivity()":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/transitivity()","title":"transitivity()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Three times the triangles over the connected triples; 0 when there are no triangles."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"transitivity"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/transitivity()"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximalCliques()":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximalcliques()","title":"maximalCliques()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximalCliques","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V","text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MaximalCliques"},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored, and an isolated vertex is a clique of one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"find_cliques"},{"type":"text","text":", igraph "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximal_cliques"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT’s Bron–Kerbosch finders)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximalCliques()","role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cl